#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:2
msgid "LIST:TRANSFORM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/include/GENEX_FAMILY.rst:3
msgid ""
"This generator expression belongs to the |genex-family| family. See that "
"section for related generator expressions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:12
msgid "Syntax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:14
msgid "$<LIST:TRANSFORM,list,ACTION[,SELECTOR]>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:20
msgid ""
"The ``list`` transformed by applying an ``ACTION`` to all or, by specifying "
"a ``SELECTOR``, to the selected list items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:25
msgid ""
"The ``TRANSFORM`` sub-command does not change the number of items in the "
"list. If a ``SELECTOR`` is specified, only some items will be changed, the "
"other ones will remain the same as before the transformation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:29
msgid ""
"``ACTION`` specifies the action to apply to the items of the list. The "
"actions have exactly the same semantics as for "
"the :command:`list(TRANSFORM)` command. ``ACTION`` must be one of the "
"following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:33
msgid ""
":command:`APPEND <list(TRANSFORM_APPEND)>`, :command:`PREPEND "
"<list(TRANSFORM_APPEND)>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:34
msgid "Append, prepend specified value to each item of the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:36
msgid "$<LIST:TRANSFORM,list,(APPEND|PREPEND),value[,SELECTOR]>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:40
msgid ""
":command:`TOLOWER <list(TRANSFORM_TOLOWER)>`, :command:`TOUPPER "
"<list(TRANSFORM_TOLOWER)>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:41
msgid "Convert each item of the list to lower, upper characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:43
msgid "$<LIST:TRANSFORM,list,(TOLOWER|TOUPPER)[,SELECTOR]>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:47
msgid ":command:`STRIP <list(TRANSFORM_STRIP)>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:48
msgid "Remove leading and trailing spaces from each item of the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:50
msgid "$<LIST:TRANSFORM,list,STRIP[,SELECTOR]>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:54
msgid ":command:`REPLACE <list(TRANSFORM_REPLACE)>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:55
msgid ""
"Match the regular expression as many times as possible and substitute the "
"replacement expression for the match for each item of the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:58
msgid "$<LIST:TRANSFORM,list,REPLACE,regular_expression,replace_expression[,SELECTOR]>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:62
msgid ""
"The ``^`` anchor now matches only at the beginning of the input element "
"instead of the beginning of each repeated search. See "
"policy :policy:`CMP0186`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:67
msgid ":command:`APPLY <list(TRANSFORM_APPLY)>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:68
msgid ""
"Transform each selected element by evaluating an arbitrary generator "
"expression ``<body>`` once per element.  Within ``<body>``, the bound "
"operand :genex:`$<_0>` expands to the current element.  Unlike the configure-"
"time :command:`list(TRANSFORM APPLY) <list(TRANSFORM_APPLY)>` command, the "
"genex form returns the body's value directly and has no side effects.  A "
"list-valued body result expands into multiple elements, like any other list-"
"valued generator expression."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:76
msgid "$<LIST:TRANSFORM,list,APPLY,body[,SELECTOR]>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:82
msgid ""
"``SELECTOR`` determines which items of the list will be transformed. Only "
"one type of selector can be specified at a time. When given, ``SELECTOR`` "
"must be one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:86
msgid "``AT``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:87
msgid "Specify a list of indexes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:89
msgid "$<LIST:TRANSFORM,list,ACTION,AT,index[,index...]>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:93
msgid "``FOR``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:94
msgid ""
"Specify a range with, optionally, an increment used to iterate over the "
"range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:97
msgid "$<LIST:TRANSFORM,list,ACTION,FOR,start,stop[,step]>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:101
msgid "``REGEX``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:102
msgid ""
"Specify a regular expression. Only items matching the regular expression "
"will be transformed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:105
msgid "$<LIST:TRANSFORM,list,ACTION,REGEX,regular_expression>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:109
msgid "``PREDICATE``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:110
msgid ""
"Specify a generator expression ``body`` evaluated once per item with the "
"bound operand :genex:`$<_0>` expanding to the current item.  Only items "
"whose body evaluates to ``1`` are transformed; the body must evaluate to "
"exactly ``0`` or ``1``.  ``PREDICATE`` may be combined with any action, "
"including ``APPLY`` (in which case both bodies bind :genex:`$<_0>` "
"independently). Like all selectors, only one selector may be given; "
"``PREDICATE`` cannot be combined with ``AT``, ``FOR``, or ``REGEX``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/LIST-TRANSFORM.rst:119
msgid "$<LIST:TRANSFORM,list,ACTION,PREDICATE,body>"
msgstr ""
